<title>USA: Lark gene fragment curtails cancer.</title>
<headline>Lark gene fragment curtails cancer.</headline>
<dateline>HOUSTON 1997-01-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Lark Technologies Inc said on Tuesday that its initial animal studies of a chromosome fragment showed the ability of the gene to reduce colon and lung cancer at statistically significant levels.</p>
<p>The company is conducting tests at the Baylor College of Medicine, Lark said.  </p>
<p>.</p>
